  "text": "Mara joins the garden and listens while Pip reads her story.\n\nBelow something, often with that thing above or covering it.\n\nFinding a number; counting on someone means relying on them.\n\nSection turned. Its short end should meet the other section.\n\nCheck these words and change anything the listener misheard.\n\nWhat does secure mean in this story, and how did they do it?\n\nPaused before doing something, often because of uncertainty.\n\nPip read The Torn Wing while Mara, Sol and Grandma listened.\n\nThe sections are joined. Does the crossing reach both banks?\n\nThe parts of your body used for holding and touching things.\n\nLoop plays the whole story and changes the pictures for you.\n\nSol is bringing his story to the garden. Mara stays at work.\n\nMara’s tape stays here. Pip is still in the present garden.\n\nPip read Mara’s story to Sol and Grandma. Mara was at work.\n\nNoticing sounds with your ears; here, listening to stories.\n\nThe bread is baked. Rina wants to take a loaf to thank Sol.\n\nAn explanation for this sentence isn't available right now.\n\nThis is the version Sol actually shared with the gathering.\n\nWatch the ending with Jo and Loop, or explore your stories.\n\nThese prepared words come from the events in Sol’s account.\n\nAn event where people gather to enjoy and share activities.\n\nRereading an earlier account · Pip stays where you left him\n\nPip read Mara’s story while Mara, Sol and Grandma listened.\n\n. Continue the show, or choose Replay story to start again.\n\nM14 7v47M22 36q-3-15 15-17-1 16-15 17Zm0 0 12-12M23 37l-2 8\n\nRina waits if you leave this path. The loaf stays with her.\n\nThe person being spoken to, or something belonging to them.\n\nThe boat is at Pip’s launch. You can unload the seed here.\n\nAsks for or refers to information about a thing or action.",
